<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sudarshan Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1859</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sudarshan Shah was the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garhwal">Garhwal</a> who regained part of his family's kingdom after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-nepalese-war">Anglo-Nepalese War</a>. His father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pradyumna-shah">Pradyumna Shah</a> had been killed fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurkhas">Gorkhas</a> in 1804; in 1815 the British restored Sudarshan Shah to the western part of Garhwal, keeping the east as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-garhwal">British Garhwal</a>. He founded Tehri as his capital and ruled Tehri Garhwal State until 1859.</p></div>
